      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your dizziness could be due to orthostatic hypotension, a possible side effect of lisinopril. It's important not to double up on your dose. Speak with your doctor about these symptoms. They can provide personalized advice, adjust your dosage, or suggest alternative medications for your blood pressure and dizziness. Aiming for bedtime versus morning medication typically depends on your specific schedule and doctor's advice. Lightheadedness when standing is more common when getting up, so perhaps setting reminders for sitting before standing could help.",
